<svelte:head><title>Language terms | Slovak Wiki</title><meta name="description" content="Plain-language definitions for grammar terms used in the Slovak Wiki."></svelte:head>

<main class="terms-page">
  <header><nav aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/grammar">Grammar</a><span>/</span><span>Language terms</span></nav><p class="eyebrow">Grammar reference</p><h1>Language terms</h1><p>Short definitions for the terms used in this reference.</p></header>

  <dl>
    <div><dt>Case</dt><dd>A word's job in a sentence, shown by its form. Slovak has six active cases.</dd><a href="/grammar/cases-overview">Open cases →</a></div>
    <div><dt>Declension</dt><dd>The set of ending changes used by nouns, adjectives, pronouns, and numerals for case, number, and gender.</dd><a href="/grammar/cases-overview">See declension through cases →</a></div>
    <div><dt>Conjugation</dt><dd>The set of verb-form changes for person, number, tense, mood, and sometimes gender.</dd><a href="/grammar/present-tense">Open present tense →</a></div>
    <div><dt>Tense</dt><dd>The time of an action: present, past, or future. Tense is one part of conjugation.</dd><a href="/grammar/present-tense">Open present tense →</a></div>
    <div><dt>Gender</dt><dd>A noun class: masculine, feminine, or neuter. Gender affects related word endings.</dd><a href="/grammar/grammatical-gender">Open grammatical gender →</a></div>
    <div><dt>Agreement</dt><dd>When related words take matching forms, such as an adjective matching a noun's gender, number, and case.</dd><a href="/grammar/grammatical-gender">See agreement →</a></div>
    <div><dt>Infinitive</dt><dd>The dictionary form of a verb: its unconjugated base form, such as rozumieť, “to understand.”</dd><a href="/grammar/present-tense">See verb forms →</a></div>
    <div><dt>Aspect</dt><dd>Whether a verb presents an action as completed or ongoing. This reference will cover it separately.</dd></div>
  </dl>
</main>

